        "question": "Who counts as a related party in a Fort Worth 1031 exchange?",
        "answer": "Related parties generally include family members defined under Section 267(b), such as siblings, spouses, ancestors, and descendants, as well as entities in which the investor holds more than fifty percent ownership. This definition applies to exchanges completed by investors in Fort Worth, TX and nationwide."
