        "question": "What is the difference between CPI linked and fixed rent bumps in a ground lease?",
        "answer": "A CPI linked escalation ties rent increases to the Consumer Price Index and can provide inflation protection, while fixed periodic bumps are negotiated at the outset and offer more predictable income modeling, and we review which structure applies to each candidate."
